t analysis.", "newValue": "Çatalhöyük is an extraordinary archaeological site in present-day Turkey, dating back to approximately 7499 BCE, representing one of the earliest urban centers in human history. Nestled between the Taurus Mountains and the Konya Plain, this settlement spans around 13 hectares and showcases a unique arrangement of mud-brick houses that reveal the social and cultural complexities of its inhabitants. The site is critical for understanding the transition from nomadic lifestyles to settled agricultural communities, offering insights into the development of social structures, trade networks, and artistic expression.

